damnableness:
中：n. damnable的变形
英：n. The state or quality of deserving damnation;
   execrableness.

debilitant:
中：[医] 致虚弱的
英：a. Diminishing the energy of organs; reducing excitement;
   as, a debilitant drug.

debonairness:
中：n. debonair,debonaire,debonnaire的变形
英：n. The quality of being debonair; good humor;
   gentleness; courtesy.

deictically:
中：adv. deictic的变形
英：adv. In a manner to show or point out; directly;
   absolutely; definitely.

demonstrableness:
中：n. demonstrable的变形
英：n. The quality of being demonstrable;
   demonstrability.

denization:
中：n. denizen的变形
英：n. The act of making one a denizen or adopted citizen;
   naturalization.

despicableness:
中：n. despicable的变形
英：n. The quality of being despicable; meanness;
   vileness; worthlessness.

dharma:
音标：/'dɑ:mә/
中：n. (佛教中的)达摩, (佛教)法, (印度教)德
英：n. basic principles of the cosmos; also: an ancient sage in Hindu mythology worshipped as a god by some lower castes;

diaphane:
中：[医] 透照灯
英：n. A woven silk stuff with transparent and colored figures;
   diaper work.

differently:
音标：/'difrentli/
中：adv. 差异, 不同, 各别, 各种
英：r. in another and different manner;

diffusiveness:
中：扩散
英：n. The quality or state of being diffusive or diffuse;
   extensiveness; expansion; dispersion. Especially of style: Diffuseness;
   want of conciseness; prolixity.

disagreeableness:
中：不愉快
英：n. The state or quality of being; disagreeable;
   unpleasantness.

discerningly:
中：有辨别力地
英：adv. In a discerning manner; with judgment; judiciously;
   acutely.

dismayedness:
中：n. dismayed的变形
英：n. A state of being dismayed; dejection of courage;
   dispiritedness.

draggle-tail:
中：n. 邋遢女人, 肮脏而不修边幅的人
英：n. A slattern who suffers her gown to trail in the mire;
   a drabble-tail.

duteous:
音标：/'dju:tjәs/
中：a. 顺从的, 尽职的
英：s willingly obedient out of a sense of duty and respect;

dutiful:
音标：/'dju:tiful/
中：a. 尽职的, 忠实的, 顺从的, 守本分的
英：s. willingly obedient out of a sense of duty and respect;

dyingness:
中：n. dying的变形
英：n. The state of dying or the stimulation of such a state;
   extreme languor; languishment.
